   0.619271         NaN   True    NaN\n4             0.2996547        NaN   0.2668273         NaN  False    NaN\n5                   NaN  0.6211338         NaN   0.5291421    NaN   True\n6             0.1345799        NaN   0.5135781         NaN   True    NaN\n7             0.1844399        NaN   0.7853351         NaN   True    NaN\n8                   NaN  0.8539753         NaN   0.4942368    NaN  False\n9                   NaN  0.8465615         NaN  0.07964548    NaN  False\n\nIn [10]: p1.dtypes\nOut[10]: \n   pivot_column\na  False           object\n   True            object\nb  False           object\n   True            object\nc  False           object\n   True            object\ndtype: object\n\nIn [11]: p1.convert_objects()\nOut[11]: \n                     a                   b                c       \npivot_column     False     True      False     True   False  True \nindex                                                             \n0             0.435995       NaN  0.025926       NaN  False    NaN\n1                  NaN  0.549662       NaN  0.435322    NaN  False\n2             0.420368       NaN  0.330335       NaN  False    NaN\n3             0.204649       NaN  0.619271       NaN   True    NaN\n4             0.299655       NaN  0.266827       NaN  False    NaN\n5                  NaN  0.621134       NaN  0.529142    NaN   True\n6             0.134580       NaN  0.513578       NaN   True    NaN\n7             0.184440       NaN  0.785335       NaN   True    NaN\n8                  NaN  0.853975       NaN  0.494237    NaN  False\n9                  NaN  0.846561       NaN  0.079645    NaN  False\n\nIn [12]: p1.convert_objects().dtypes\nOut[12]: \n   pivot_column\na  False           float64\n   True            float64\nb  False           float64\n   True            float64\nc  False            object\n   True             object\ndtype: object\n\n```\n\nSimple enough to do a `.convert_objects()` to convert what can be (and that maybe the soln; haven't really looked internally). When you pivot the frame it is mixed to begin with because you are including float and boolean columns; that's why its `object`, but I agree, should be coerced back.\n\nNote that the 'c' columns WILL remain as bool because they have `nan` (you can always `.fillna(False)` if you wanted).\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pandas-dev/pandas/issues/comments/43358601/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"jreback","id":953992,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk1Mzk5Mg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/953992?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jreback","html_url":"https://github.com/jreback","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jreback/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jreback/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jreback/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jreback/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jreback/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jreback/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jreback/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jreback/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jreback/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"id":121987656,"node_id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDEyMTk4NzY1Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pandas-dev/pandas/issues/events/121987656","actor":{"login":"jreback","id":953992,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk1Mzk5Mg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/953992?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jreback","html_url":"https://github.com/jreback","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jreback/followers","following_url":"https: